{"id":"int-1ecc215d5a262a486fc8540806d2288e","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-12T22:46:26.549087Z","actor":"Jakob Priesner","issue_id":"culina-v2-2si","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Phase 8 complete. The list merges amounts, groups by shop section with per-household corrections, takes a recipe at the yield on screen, and survives two people writing to it at once."}}
{"id":"int-f98a9e0cfd689743a366f71991bf1ae9","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-12T22:54:49.092099Z","actor":"Jakob Priesner","issue_id":"culina-v2-4zj","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Hand-written service worker on SvelteKit's $service-worker instead of @vite-pwa/sveltekit: no svelte.config.js in this project, injectManifest semantics come free, and the file is short enough to read. Precaches the shell per build, answers navigations from cache, never caches /api, and defers skipWaiting to a culina:activate message from the page with a non-expiring update toast. Covered by tests/e2e/pwa.spec.ts and src/lib/app/updates.spec.ts. Install prompt verified against the manifest; Lighthouse run deferred to the packaged container."}}
{"id":"int-d6afbaa7770c3bdbbcc0938f71b5ce0c","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-12T23:12:51.044904Z","actor":"Jakob Priesner","issue_id":"culina-v2-uqm","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"A recipe that has been opened stays readable and cookable offline: allow-listed stale-while-revalidate for the recipe, cache-first for its image, network-first for the list, plus /users/me so a cold offline start can tell 'offline' from 'signed out'. Cleared on sign-in and sign-out. Offline badge in the shell and client-side failures now speak the reader's language via $shell/explain. Deviation from the sketch: mutating controls are not disabled offline — they stay tappable and the app says 'You are offline. This will be possible again when you reconnect.' A disabled control with no explanation is worse than a control that explains itself, and the editor keeps its draft either way. Covered by tests/e2e/pwa.spec.ts."}}
{"id":"int-90eaa2cbee0b86d623f1e33f0494fc98","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-12T23:17:31.752184Z","actor":"Jakob Priesner","issue_id":"culina-v2-78r","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Three-stage Dockerfile at the repo root. Built, run against a real database, and verified: migrations applied at boot, /health/ready 200, the SPA served at / and on a deep link, the service worker served no-cache, and Docker reporting the container healthy. 197 MB against the ~250 MB target. Two things the bead did not anticipate: NuGet lock files did not exist, so RestorePackagesWithLockFile is now on (excluded for the .slnx, which has no target framework and makes NuGet refuse the restore); and the chiseled runtime has no shell or curl, so the HEALTHCHECK is the app itself — Api --health-check makes one request to /health/ready and exits 0 or 1, the same pattern as --export-openapi. The root .editorconfig has to be in the build context: EnforceCodeStyleInBuild plus warnings-as-errors makes a missing one a failed build."}}
{"id":"int-fc0607fb17cad714f46c1c764313faac","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-12T23:22:19.341857Z","actor":"Jakob Priesner","issue_id":"culina-v2-jlb","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"compose.prod.yaml layers over compose.yaml: database port removed (!override []), read_only with tmpfs /tmp, no-new-privileges, cap_drop ALL, named volumes for /data/images and /data/keys with a loud comment on each, depends_on service_healthy, and the image's own --health-check. Verified from an empty volume: db healthy, app healthy, migrations 0001-0006 applied, deep link served, first account created. Removed the fixed container_name from both files — it made the compose files unusable for two projects at once, which is exactly the situation when checking a production compose against a running development one. .env.example gained ForwardedHeaders__KnownNetworks."}}
{"id":"int-857747a77f2eba6d40c4beb432b97a04","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-09-12T23:26:13.428501Z","actor":"Jakob Priesner","issue_id":"culina-v2-hlw","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"ci.yml (backend, frontend, contract, e2e, codeql, security), release.yml (tag-triggered multi-arch build, SBOM, keyless cosign signature and attestation, build provenance, generated notes) and nightly.yml (published-image rescan plus dependency audit). Validated with actionlint. Every action pinned to a commit SHA resolved from the GitHub API, with the version in a trailing comment. Not yet observed running: this repository has no remote configured, so the first push will be the first execution."}}
